 :statement "$T Y T^\\dagger = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(Y - X)$: Computing $T Y T^\\dagger = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\omega \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 0 & -i \\\\ i & 0 \\end{pmatrix} \\begin{pmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\omega^* \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 0 & -i\\omega^* \\\\ i\\omega & 0 \\end{pmatrix}$. Since $i\\omega = ie^{i\\pi/4} = e^{i\\pi/2}e^{i\\pi/4} = e^{i3\\pi/4} = \\frac{-1+i}{\\sqrt{2}}$ and $-i\\omega^* = -ie^{-i\\pi/4} = e^{-i3\\pi/4} = \\frac{-1-i}{\\sqrt{2}}$, we get $\\begin{pmatrix} 0 & \\frac{-1-i}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{-1+i}{\\sqrt{2}} & 0 \\end{pmatrix} = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\left( \\begin{pmatrix} 0 & -i \\\\ i & 0 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\end{pmatrix} \\right) = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}(Y - X)$."
